%N A402135 Decimal expansion of the total perimeter of the trefoil curve.
%C A402135 The curve is defined by x^4+x^2*y^2+y^4=x*(x^2-y^2). The perimeter includes all three lobes.
%C A402135 A rational parametrization is x=(1-t^2)/(1+t^2+t^4), y=t*(1-t^2)/(1+t^2+t^4), for -infinity<t<infinity.
%H A402135 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TrefoilCurve.html">Trefoil Curve</a>.
%F A402135 Equals 2*Integral_{t=0..infinity} sqrt(1+8*t^2+40*t^4+34*t^6-8*t^8-4*t^10+t^12)/(1+t^2+t^4)^2 dt.
%e A402135 3.83680354329460136337870579997497710573108895946885...
%t A402135 RealDigits[2 NIntegrate[Sqrt[1 + 8 t^2 + 40 t^4 + 34 t^6 - 8 t^8 - 4 t^10 + t^12]/(1 + t^2 + t^4)^2, {t, 0, 1, Infinity}, WorkingPrecision -> 120, PrecisionGoal -> 105], 10, 87][[1]]
%K A402135 nonn,cons,new
